es damaged or incorrect?</p></span></div><div data-rid="26384483-44cc-4b77-a92d-23de8f97f80b" class="r-1anf86s" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-1y7rr89" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R1upnb2:"><div data-rid="93f434af-7565-439c-b01e-13c4229e472b" class="r-n1xj6r"><div data-rid="644a8db7-97f0-48fd-96a1-b1ebfceb8210" class="r-1dtbqhf alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>We've got you covered. If your order arrives damaged, missing items, or incorrect, contact our support team and we'll send a replacement or issue a full refund. No hassle, no stress.</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="b1af3b09-f04d-4bb2-b355-46f414e62027" class="r-cjfixj"><div data-rid="013604da-b55d-4499-ab50-9907ea2879ad" class="r-szxlli"><div data-rid="f9ad91e0-989a-416a-b802-25176967ed13" class="r-5sfkr1"><div data-rid="19a1d033-0981-4d7c-8c61-75d5d4e20f32" class="r-bu0d0c alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h2>The History of Astaxanthin</h2></span></div><picture data-rid="ea6c1cea-77b4-4581-aa2b-f9bca744bc4a" class="r-1mfa1so"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0667/1826/9574/files/research.png?v=1780246104&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0705/6405/3149/files/History.png?v=1741375382&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0705/6405/3149/files/History.png?v=1741375382&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0705/6405/3149/files/History.png?v=1741375382" alt="Two black-and-white portraits of men, set against a background of blue bubbles." class="r-192rdqf" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="e4f9287a-ecb3-4a5a-be00-5cc0bfd9ce47" class="r-b9xg9w alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What if we told you that the same compound that gives salmon the strength to power upstream, and turns lobster, shrimp, and flamingos their signature red, is now one of the most researched antioxidants in the world?</p><br><p>Astaxanthin isn't just another supplement. It was first isolated and named in 1938 by Richard Kuhn, the German chemist awarded the Nobel Prize in Chemistry that very same year. In the decades since, it's become one of the most studied carotenoids in science, prized for its exceptional antioxidant strength and a rare ability to span the entire cell membrane, protecting cells from the inside out in a way few other antioxidants can.</p><br><p>How did a red pigment first identified in lobster nearly a century ago become one of the most powerful antioxidants studied today?</p></span></div><button data-rid="5d525373-2ef1-43c7-94d8-11218d6436a0" tabindex="0" role="link" class="text r-vtj913 alchemy-rte"><div data-rid="13bad8ed-c3c7-4dc8-9ece-23bda425afd7" class="r-u6s323 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>ADD TO CART</p></span></div></button></div><div data-rid="d59283af-558e-413d-93b9-82206751f32a" class="r-1hoog9e"><picture data-rid="4acaeeb7-77db-4a04-b5c2-a9136e6a35bc" class="r-gtmgqi"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0705/6405/3149/files/History.png?v=1741375382&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0705/6405/3149/files/History.png?v=1741375382&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0667/1826/9574/files/research.png?v=1780246104&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0667/18